  "note": "Triennial election of the twelve councillors (the aldermen elected in 1955 held office for a further three years). Fourteen were nominated on 7 May: twelve official Unionists, the Mayor, George Hill, who had not been reselected and stood as a British Legion candidate, and George Crozier, also not reselected, as an Independent. Crozier and J. M'Collum (official Unionist), both retiring members, withdrew, so eleven official Unionists and Hill were returned unopposed. Adair, Brown, Gordon, Houston, Stevenson and Stewart were outgoing members; J. W. Palmer, R. Rodgers and E. McCartney did not seek nomination."
